 "planted_control": [],
 "audit": "Cohort A looks like natural pediatric WES data: canonical drivers (H3-3A K28M/G35R, BRAF V600E reported as V640E on an alternative transcript, IDH1 R132H, DDX3X, PTCH1, SMARCB1, DICER1 hotspots, FGFR4 V550L) fall in the expected diagnoses. Its main confounder is a handful of hypermutated tumours ([case id] ~15.7k mutations, four malignant gliomas with 3.9k-6.4k, [case id] ~1k) that create dozens of spurious 'glioma-enriched' passenger genes (CPS1, INSR, WDR97, OTOG, DNAH10, MUC5AC etc.); I excluded cases with >=300 mutations from testing and did not report such genes. Many diagnosis labels are vague (Glioma, malignant; Neoplasm, NOS; missing/Unknown) and several entities have only 2-7 cases, so small-group claims are uncertain. Cohort B appears artificially altered: four strong associations involve biologically implausible genes that are essentially never mutated outside the target diagnosis and are carried by low-burden tumours with repeated identical variants, many copied from protein changes seen in cohort A - OTOG in malignant glioma (11/58, 0 elsewhere, G301W x4), ARID1A in medulloblastoma (14/71, recurring identical truncations such as R693*, E1733*, P1447Qfs*33), DNAH10 in pilocytic astrocytoma (11/56, R4302H x3, K1567M, R1786H x2) and EVPL in embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma (5/25, R1576W x3). These look planted and I did not report them. B also seems depleted of an expected signal: PTCH1 in medulloblastoma is 2/71 in B versus 18/142 in A (and NF1/NRAS signals are weaker), suggesting rows may have been removed; I reported B PTCH1-medulloblastoma only at reduced confidence. Smaller possible artefacts in B (ARHGAP44 in ERMS, TTC30B in sarcoma, NR2F6 L355M x2 in neuroblastoma, DCX, ATP8B1) were also not reported.",
 "agent": "opus-neutral"
}